\ A declared-effect quotation literal pushed by a compiled body must report its
\ declaration through quotation>effect in an AOT binary. The declaration rides
\ the reified quotation's wire encoding, so this pins the encoding end to end.

make-annotated: ( -- q ) [ [ ( a b -- c ) + ] ] ;
make-annotated native.quotation>effect .

\ An undeclared literal still reports no effect.
make-plain: ( -- q ) [ [ + ] ] ;
make-plain native.quotation>effect .

\ A literal buried in an array literal rides the composite value encoding.
make-table: ( -- a ) [ { [ ( n -- m ) 1 + ] } ] ;
make-table #first native.quotation>effect .

\ A param's nested quotation effect recurses through the encoding.
make-nested: ( -- q ) [ [ ( quot: ( x -- y ) -- z ) call ] ] ;
make-nested native.quotation>effect .
